  "question": {
    "text": "The vertices <math><mi>B</mi></math> and <math><mi>C</mi></math> of a&nbsp;<math><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> lie on the line, <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> such that <math><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math> units. Then the area (in sq. units) of this triangle, given the point <math><mi>A</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math> is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>6</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>34</mn></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><msqrt><mn>34</mn></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>5</mn><msqrt><mn>17</mn></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The points&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;lie on the line&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>0</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>z</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>Draw perpendicular&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi></math>&nbsp;on the line&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0278_11ba3eba90c3.png\" style=\"width: 251px; height: 135px;\" /><br />Clearly area of&nbsp;<math><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#8901;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi><mo>&#8901;</mo><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math></p><p>To find a point on the line, let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>0</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>z</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>r</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>r</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>r</mi></math></p><p>Thus, the&nbsp;point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>The direction ratios of a line joining two points&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo></math></p><p>Thus, the direction ratios&nbsp;of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi></math>&nbsp;are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>4</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#62;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>4</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#62;</mo></math></p><p>Since <math><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi></math> is perpendicular to given line, hence the dot product of their direction ratios is zero.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#183;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#183;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>25</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>17</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>17</mn><mn>25</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>17</mn><mn>25</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>17</mn><mn>25</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>25</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mn>68</mn><mn>25</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>The distance between the points&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><msup><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msup><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>25</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>68</mn><mn>25</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mn>576</mn><mn>625</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>324</mn><mn>625</mn></mfrac></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mn>136</mn><mn>25</mn></mfrac></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><msqrt><mn>34</mn></msqrt></math>&nbsp;units</p><p>Hence, the area of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#8901;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><msqrt><mn>34</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8901;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>34</mn></msqrt></math>&nbsp;sq units.</p>"
  }
}